# Default Haunted Skeleton Model

This is the default placeholder for the Phantom Engine standard skeleton model.

# Phantom Engine Default Skeleton Asset

This is a default placeholder skeleton model for the Phantom Engine.

For production use, replace this with actual `.gltf` or `.obj` skeleton files
from Mixamo, Blender, or Sketchfab.

## Expected Format

The engine supports:
- `.gltf` / `.glb` - Binary and JSON container formats with embedded geometry
- `.obj` - Wavefront OBJ format

## Bone Hierarchy Requirements

The skeleton must follow a hierarchical structure with:
1. Root bone (pelvis/hip)
2. Spine chain (hip -> spine -> chest)
3. Upper limb chains (clavicle -> upper arm -> forearm -> hand)
4. Lower limb chains (femur -> tibia -> fibula -> foot)
5. Neck and head chain

## Calibration

Use the in-app calibration tools to align MediaPipe keypoints to the imported skeleton.
